         "other_defensible_labels": [],
         "defect": "The item is well posed with C as the single correct choice. A is wrong because all three samples were measured at the same 25°C, so collision frequency should be the same in each. B is wrong because the enzyme was incubated without substrate, and fresh substrate was added afterward. D is wrong because denaturation disrupts noncovalent interactions that hold the enzyme's shape; it does not necessarily break peptide bonds. C correctly links the low rate to heat-disrupted interactions that alter the active site, an effect that persists after cooling."
        },
